report.summary:
I fixed every review item (both mediums and all lows), added most of the missing scope, and re-ran everything. Typecheck is clean for my files. The realism tests pass: 34 passed, with 14 that only run in strict mode. The Python self-test passes 28 of 28. All 122 checked audit values reproduce within tolerance. I made no edits outside my files.

**The two medium items:**
- **Drill reloading.** Typing in the reader field or answering no longer reloads the frames, restarts playback or flashes the loading overlay. The reaction-time clock now starts once per trial. The two clips are built once per trial in `RealOrSimDrill.tsx`, and the player reloads only when the clip names change.
- **Capture mode.** Captures now call `setCaptureMode(true)` and pass `framesSinceStart` and `mode` on every frame, so a slow upload can no longer restart a run. I re-ran the determinism check in my own browser tab, which I closed afterwards. Four captures of the same 8 frames gave identical hashes on every frame: two with normal uploads, one with each upload delayed 600 ms (longer than the renderer's 400 ms run-gap rule), and one with no upload.

**Low items:**
- **Pre-contrast local contrast.** It is now measured on a frame with coronary iodine at or below 1% of the peak. If there is no such frame, the scorecard shows n/a instead of a wrong value. In the current lab it is n/a, because frame 0 already holds about 2%.
- **Noise-by-grey rows** are scored against cd-ds, and the label says so. The cd-main bands are attached to each row for comparison.
- **Reproduction tolerances.** Each row now stores its tolerance, a strict 5% flag and a pass flag. Only rho uses a wider tolerance, because the published value 0.08 is rounded to two decimals; the harness gets 0.084.
- **Silent fallback.** Captures now stop with an error if the scene builder stops supplying the heart-surface mapping, instead of producing plausible-looking garbage.
- **Gate scale.** The test gates now predict the same field box as the Python side (the lab's square field fills the canvas). Captures are 0.280 mm per 512-px pixel against the library's 0.3077, 9% finer, and a test keeps them within 15%.
- **CADICA error.** The single-frame CADICA run is now a recorded skip: 0 errors, 1 skip.
- **RealAngiograms diff.** I rebased it on the current file, which now has the "progress" tab.

**Missing scope added:**
- **New scorecard rows** (via a new `geometry.py`):
  - tortuosity in three bands, LM+LAD length and tree extent;
  - landmark motion in mm, and speeds in mm/s;
  - contrast arrival at 30% of the rise, and whether contrast is present in the first frame;
  - a fluoro-versus-cine noise rule: fluoro must be noisier at equal grey.
- **Where the real values come from.** The geometry targets re-use the anatomy audit's saved results with Python ports of its code. They reproduce its published numbers: 11.2° tortuosity, 135 mm length, 17.8 / 8.2 mm motion, 48 / 17 mm/s speeds (harness 49.4 / 16.8) and the four tree extents.
- **New test gates:**
  - LAD/LCx climb over the first 20 mm, strict mode only;
  - the Finet ratio, printed beside the literature mean 0.678 but not asserted;
  - the mm-per-pixel scale check.
  - Finet 2008 is cited from the Europe PMC record; PubMed only returned a cookie notice.
- **Capture options.** Captures accept an imaging-system `profile`.
- **Per-view targets.** Timing, arrival, local contrast, opacified area, block motion and cross-section tracks are now split per artery and view family. The scorecard uses the view-specific target when it has at least 3 real runs. The targets file grew from 683 to 1,765 targets.

**New baseline.** The standard capture set (`s0base`) is now the plan's five views plus RAO cranial, with a 40-frame fluoro companion. It scores 133 of 229 metrics inside the real band on the matched pipeline and 137 of 229 lossless. The largest gaps, with owners:
- lung texture is too faint (S4);
- the left coronary fills too fast and washes out below baseline (S5/S10);
- the opacified area is too small (S3b/S5);
- the vessels move in jumps, with median landmark speed 2.7-4.2 mm/s against 10-26 (S3a);
- the catheter does not move with the heart (S7);
- vessel profiles are too wide and flat-topped (S2b);
- the left tree is 49-52 mm wide against 64-131 (S3b);
- the RCA RAO view is too bright (S2).

**Cost.** Nothing in the shipped lab. In capture mode at 768 px, building a scene takes 0.7-2.0 ms and rendering with read-back 12-21 ms per frame.
